# Self-Hosted Docker Code Execution Engine

Replace the broken Piston public API with a secure, self-hosted execution pipeline.  
User code is run inside a **ephemeral Docker container** spun up by the Node.js backend — isolated, time-limited, and with no external API dependency.

## Architecture

```
React Frontend
    ↓  POST /api/execute  { language, code }
Node.js Backend  (new route + controller)
    ↓  dockerode  (Node.js Docker SDK)
Ephemeral Docker Container  (python / node / openjdk image)
    ↓  stdout / stderr
Backend returns  { success, output, error }
    ↓
React displays result
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Docker Desktop must be running** on the machine where the backend runs. Verify with `docker --version` before we start.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Backend

#### [NEW] `executeRoutes.js` — [NEW](file:///Users/kishorekumar/Documents/Projects/HireSync/backend/src/routes/executeRoutes.js)

A single route, **no auth guard** (execution is stateless and sandboxed):

```
POST /api/execute
Body: { language: "python" | "javascript" | "java", code: "..." }
```

---

#### [NEW] `executeController.js` — [NEW](file:///Users/kishorekumar/Documents/Projects/HireSync/backend/src/controllers/executeController.js)

Core logic using the `dockerode` npm package:

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| 1 | Validate `language` and `code` |
| 2 | Map language → Docker image + run command |
| 3 | `docker.createContainer(...)` with `NetworkDisabled: true`, memory/CPU limits |
| 4 | Write code to container's stdin or via bind-mount temp file |
| 5 | Start container, collect stdout/stderr stream |
| 6 | Kill + remove container after **5 second timeout** |
| 7 | Return `{ success, output, error }` |

**Docker image map:**

| Language | Image | Run command |
|---|---|---|
| `javascript` | `node:18-alpine` | `node /code/main.js` |
| `python` | `python:3.11-slim` | `python /code/main.py` |
| `java` | `openjdk:17-slim` | `javac /code/Main.java && java -cp /code Main` |

**Container security config:**
```js
{
  NetworkDisabled: true,      // no internet access
  Memory: 128 * 1024 * 1024, // 128 MB RAM cap
  CpuQuota: 50000,            // 50% of 1 CPU
  ReadonlyRootfs: false,      // need to write temp file
  AutoRemove: true,           // auto-cleanup on exit
}
```

---

#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///Users/kishorekumar/Documents/Projects/HireSync/backend/src/server.js) — [server.js](file:///Users/kishorekumar/Documents/Projects/HireSync/backend/src/server.js)

